  "pragmaticFunctions": {
    "_comment": "A learner who masters every category above can describe a room and state facts about their day, but cannot politely ask a stranger for anything. A language-pedagogy review found the gap directly in beginner-expressible.test.ts: of ~65 canonical sentences, not one was a request ('give me...'), a permission question ('can I...?'), an invitation, an agree/disagree exchange, or a repair strategy beyond a single fixed phrase. `closedClasses.politeness` covers greeting, farewell, thanks and one apology token and stops there - a reasonable floor, but nothing past it. These are the Council of Europe Threshold level / Instituto Cervantes PCIC A1-A2 'funciones' every first conversation actually needs, grouped by SPEECH ACT rather than by semantic domain the way `verbFunctions` is, because that is the axis the gap was found on. Entries here are the natural spoken phrase, not a textbook citation form - Catalan speakers say 'endavant' to grant permission and 'no puc' to decline, not a translated 'you may' or 'I am unable to'. `seure` is listed explicitly because the expressibility test asserts \"Puc seure aquí?\" and the draft's spec did not require it - it passed only because the old whitespace split in tag-beginner-core tagged it incidentally. Once that split was fixed the tag went away and the sentence failed, which is the checker working: a sentence the test claims a beginner can say has to be a sentence the spec actually requires the words for.",
    "requestingFavour": [
      "voldria",
      "podries",
      "un moment",
      "un favor"
    ],
    "permission": [
      "puc",
      "es pot",
      "no es pot",
      "endavant",
      "seure"
    ],
    "offeringInviting": [
      "vols",
      "t'agradaria",
      "vine",
      "convidar"
    ],
    "acceptingDeclining": [
      "d'acord",
      "amb molt de gust",
      "no puc",
      "acceptar"
    ],
    "agreeingDisagreeing": [
      "estic d'acord",
      "no estic d'acord",
      "tens raó",
      "és veritat"
    ],
    "suggesting": [
      "i si",
      "què et sembla",
      "podríem",
      "millor anem"
    ],
    "repair": [
      "pots repetir",
      "més a poc a poc",
      "no entenc",
      "què vol dir",
      "com es diu"
    ],
    "apologising": [
      "perdona",
      "ho sento",
      "no passa res",
      "no et preocupis"
    ]
  }
